@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant — requirement graph vs traceability matrix (adjacency table).
'   usecase:      Note when each representation is clearer.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       systems-engineering
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Requirement - Graph vs Traceability Matrix (Variant)

' Two representations of the same set: {REQ-A, REQ-B} derived from {ROOT},
' satisfied by {B1, B2}, verified by {T1, T2}.

' ---- Part 1: Requirement graph ------------------------------------------
' Best when: exploring unknown links, finding coverage gaps visually,
' presenting to a stakeholder audience.

class "ROOT" <<requirement>> { id : REQ-R }
class "REQ-A" <<requirement>> { id : REQ-A1 }
class "REQ-B" <<requirement>> { id : REQ-B1 }
class "Block1" <<block>>
class "Block2" <<block>>
class "Test1" <<testCase>> { id : T1 }
class "Test2" <<testCase>> { id : T2 }

"REQ-A" ..> "ROOT" : <<deriveReqt>>
"REQ-B" ..> "ROOT" : <<deriveReqt>>
"Block1" ..> "REQ-A" : <<satisfy>>
"Block2" ..> "REQ-B" : <<satisfy>>
"Test1" ..> "REQ-A" : <<verify>>
"Test2" ..> "REQ-B" : <<verify>>

note right of "ROOT"
  <b>Graph view — best when:</b>
  - Few requirements, rich topology
  - Reading paths/traces aloud
  - Spotting orphan requirements
  - Stakeholder review
end note

' ---- Part 2: Traceability matrix (adjacency table) ---------------------
' Best when: scale is large (hundreds+ reqs), auditing coverage cell-by-cell,
' generating a compliance report, or feeding a tool that consumes tables.

note bottom of "REQ-B"
  <b>Matrix view — best when:</b>
  - Hundreds/thousands of requirements
  - Auditing coverage cell-by-cell
  - Compliance reporting (X cell empty = gap)
  - Tabular tooling (DOORS, Jama, etc.)
end note

@enduml

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' The matrix below is intentionally shown as a code block in this comment so
' the converter can render it as a separate diagram view or a sibling asset.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
'
' Traceability Matrix (adjacency):
'
'              | deriveReqt | satisfy | verify
' -------------|------------|---------|--------
'  REQ-A       |    ROOT    | Block1  |  T1
'  REQ-B       |    ROOT    | Block2  |  T2
'  ROOT        |     -      |    -    |  -
'
' Empty cells (ROOT satisfy/verify) signal coverage gaps the graph obscures
' at scale but the matrix surfaces immediately.
